{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/570917-conspiracies-and-their-dark-secrets","id":570917,"title":"Conspiracies and their Dark Secrets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-27T21:57:52-07:00","id":570917,"title":"Conspiracies and their Dark Secrets","content":"Not everyone loves them, but I'm personally a big fan of the flaws presented in the various conspiracies. What I'm curious about is how people have actually incorporated them into their games.<br /> <br /> For example, when using Task Force Valkyrie I've handled them one of three ways:<br /> <br /> 1) The upper echelons of the organization have been compromised by their dependence on cash flow from vampires. However the bloodsuckers influence is not as pervasive as it would appear. The shadowy nature of the conspiracy and it's byzantine bureaucracy mean that the interloping vampires don't have a complete sense of what they have their fingers in, and one hidden financier is not necessarily aware of the others' existence. Were they to wield their leverage together they could turn the agency into their pawns, but for the most part they lack the awareness to do so.<br /> <br /> 2) Layer after layer of the conspiracy peels back to reveal more deception and riddles. The agency is directed by a smoke-filled room of Cold War spooks. They in turn take their orders from a cabal of vampires within the Invictus. They in turn are infiltrated by deep cover initiates of the mysterious group known as VII.<br /> <br /> 3) The entirety of Valkyrie has been suborned by the influence of vampires. You know the truth, and your cell seems clean, but can you keep the Vigil while still keeping one eye on your own organization? You know there have to be others like you left, you just have to find them. If you can secretly gather enough of an insurgency you might be able to take back Valkyrie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T03:18:58-07:00","id":571109,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I feel the intent was 2, but that doesn't vmean that the PCs don't think it's 3.<br /> <br /> I figure they're called conspiracies for a reason-lies, dark secrets, trust issues. Valkyrie takes blood money, cheiron is run by aliens, the inquisition is run by a ghoul, what is the lady lucifuge up to, AO includes terrorists and drug lords, who are the patrons of the cainite heresy, etc, etc. <br /> <br /> They're story hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T03:57:38-07:00","id":571147,"title":"","content":"I think there may be a fair contigent of people who have simply ignored the vampire stuff in TFV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T04:42:27-07:00","id":571175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/570917-conspiracies-and-their-dark-secrets?p=571147#post571147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there may be a fair contigent of people who have simply ignored the vampire stuff in TFV.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's their right, should they find it conflicts with their ideas/plans for TFV in their chronicle. But I don't think the vampire conspiracy stuff is necessarily a bad idea, in fact I think it makes for a great chronicle plot, if you work it right and keep it all very tinker tailor soldier vampire or &quot;you can't handle the truth!&quot;. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Have you seen him? </i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1000-mistere","name":"MisterE","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1000_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T04:46:30-07:00","id":571181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/570917-conspiracies-and-their-dark-secrets?p=571147#post571147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there may be a fair contigent of people who have simply ignored the vampire stuff in TFV.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Clashes directly with hunters core themes of united we stand and strength in numbers.<br /> <br /> Plus it must be the most boring secret truth ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T05:28:55-07:00","id":571224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/570917-conspiracies-and-their-dark-secrets?p=571181#post571181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. Clashes directly with hunters core themes of united we stand and strength in numbers.<br /> <br /> Plus it must be the most boring secret truth ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. If I ever use it, I have it that it's actually the <i>least </i>deviant from it's own mission; the vampires who fund it are all ex-members and American patriots, led by a Northern hero of the Civil War who hates the way his fellows treat ghouls (&quot;I died the first time for ending slavery. I figure I might as well spend my undeath doing the same thing; reminds me of being a human soldier&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T05:32:18-07:00","id":571226,"title":"","content":"Come on man; you cannot do that without having a vampire Abraham Lincon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T08:30:42-07:00","id":571425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/570917-conspiracies-and-their-dark-secrets?p=571181#post571181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. Clashes directly with hunters core themes of united we stand and strength in numbers.<br /> <br /> Plus it must be the most boring secret truth ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. I've never found unity to be at all a theme in Hunter. It's such a kitchen sink game of different approaches and moods that making them the super friends feels like a cop out. If all the groups work together and all have completely pure motivations then at that point they've basically won. The point of the conspiracies in particular is the trade off between being able to beat monsters at their own game and the fact that you've done so by becoming just like them.<br /> <br /> Also, the award for most boring secret has to go to the Loyalists of Thule. &quot;We think its pretty okay to kill Nazis...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T08:37:11-07:00","id":571459,"title":"","content":"Oh, I never said all the groups work together. Quite the opposite. I said that your group works together - case in point. The core &quot;power&quot; of Hunters is Tactics, which are powered by teamwork.<br /> <br /> (The Loyalists of Thule's Nazi origin wasn't a secret)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T13:14:13-07:00","id":571804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/570917-conspiracies-and-their-dark-secrets?p=571459#post571459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I never said all the groups work together. Quite the opposite. I said that your group works together - case in point. The core &quot;power&quot; of Hunters is Tactics, which are powered by teamwork.<br /> <br /> (The Loyalists of Thule's Nazi origin wasn't a secret)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair.<br /> <br /> Their origin as a Nazi-affiliated group wasn't a secret, but treated as one of the organization's &quot;dirty secrets&quot; is that they're okay with killing mortal Neo-Nazis. Sure, I get that at that point you're talking about murder more so than in the case of the supernatural, but it still never struck me as being particularly sordid. <br /> <br /> In any case: If somebody doesn't want to use the material that's their game (and their loss in my opinion). I was curious how people who 'did' want to use the material had incorporated it into their games.<br /> <br /> For another example, my take on the Cheiron Group kind of runs between the two versions presented in C&amp;C. The creatures that make up the board of directors are genuinely on the side of light, or at least something close to it, trying to save the world from the doom that consumed their universe. They're still alien beings though, and their sense of right and wrong doesn't always line up with ours. What they're willing to do in order to defeat the darkness might have a cost we aren't willing to pay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T13:54:25-07:00","id":571850,"title":"","content":"My take on Cheiron is vastly different. The Board of Directors are entirely mundane humans who have a business deal with the demigod centaur Cheiron. They ensure he has <i>lots</i> of sacrifices; and in return the moment a doctor signs an employment contract with Cheiron they get +2 dots of Medicine.<br /> <br /> Most of the company doesn't have a clue. The middle manager thinks that if he cuts corners and sends hunters out with less equipment he can use that money to fund a skunkworks research project into his daughter's rare disease. The doctor just thinks that if he cuts up this monster he'll be able to create new cures. Cheiron is full of good people and a corporate structure that turns their good intentions into something purely evil.<br /> <br /> In reality the monster and the under equipped hunters are both the sacrifices that keep the deal going. The hunters filled with Thamatology are the Heroes who's legends become another strand in the Trainer of Heroes' mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T17:20:51-07:00","id":572019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/570917-conspiracies-and-their-dark-secrets?p=571850#post571850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take on Cheiron is vastly different. The Board of Directors are entirely mundane humans who have a business deal with the demigod centaur Cheiron. They ensure he has <i>lots</i> of sacrifices; and in return the moment a doctor signs an employment contract with Cheiron they get +2 dots of Medicine.<br /> <br /> Most of the company doesn't have a clue. The middle manager thinks that if he cuts corners and sends hunters out with less equipment he can use that money to fund a skunkworks research project into his daughter's rare disease. The doctor just thinks that if he cuts up this monster he'll be able to create new cures. Cheiron is full of good people and a corporate structure that turns their good intentions into something purely evil.<br /> <br /> In reality the monster and the under equipped hunters are both the sacrifices that keep the deal going. The hunters filled with Thamatology are the Heroes who's legends become another strand in the Trainer of Heroes' mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is also cool. I like it. <br /> <br /> I also tend to work in a Promethean angle with Cheiron Group. They both work well in the realm of body horror and the idea of a misguided hunter becoming more Thaumatech than flesh dovetails too perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T06:25:13-07:00","id":573863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/570917-conspiracies-and-their-dark-secrets?p=571850#post571850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take on Cheiron is vastly different. The Board of Directors are entirely mundane humans who have a business deal with the demigod centaur Cheiron. They ensure he has <i>lots</i> of sacrifices; and in return the moment a doctor signs an employment contract with Cheiron they get +2 dots of Medicine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've really run roughly the same in my head canon.Cherion got started off as a compact of doctors who saw things that were going bump in the night and decided to so something about it. For most of Cheiron's history, they were mostly altruistic until the profit motive start kicking in. Now the doctors who now compose the Board of Directors are simply doctors who turned to turning themselves into monsters and cling to Cheiron simply because they don't want to die or live the half lives that Kindred do.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}